## 4. Vary: Accept-Language
   concept: one URL, two languages: the cache keys entries on the request header the response names in Vary, normalised to the language the origin will pick, so 6 spellings make 2 entries
   Accept-Language: en-GB,en;q=0.9             -> HIT  Content-Language: en  How contributions work
   Accept-Language: fr-FR,fr;q=0.9,en;q=0.8    -> HIT  Content-Language: fr  Comment fonctionnent les cotisations
   Accept-Language: fr                         -> HIT  Content-Language: fr  Comment fonctionnent les cotisations
   Accept-Language: en-US,en;q=0.9             -> HIT  Content-Language: en  How contributions work
   Accept-Language: fr-CA,fr;q=0.9,en;q=0.7    -> HIT  Content-Language: fr  Comment fonctionnent les cotisations
   Accept-Language: de-DE,de;q=0.9,en;q=0.5    -> HIT  Content-Language: en  How contributions work
   ok   two entries for the help page (en, fr), each served to the right readers

## 5. The privacy bug: a personal page cached as public
   concept: a build sends Cache-Control: public on /members/me (and drops Vary on the help page); the URL is the same for every member, so the shared cache hands member 1's page to member 2
   [origin] member pages and API on :53054 (BUGGY build: personal pages public, help page without Vary)
   [cache] purge everything: 5 entries
   member 1 (Alice) opens /members/me: Alice Martin  [MISS, Cache-Control: public, max-age=300]
   member 2 (Bruno) opens /members/me: Alice Martin  [HIT]  <- Alice's name, IBAN and balance
   ok   with the buggy header the shared cache serves member 1's page to member 2
   without Vary: an English reader fills the entry, then a French reader gets How contributions work [HIT]
   ok   without Vary the French reader gets the English page
   deploy the fix (private, no-cache; Vary back) ...
   [origin] member pages and API on :53054
   member 2 right after the deploy: Alice Martin [HIT]  <- the leaked entry is still fresh for 300 s
   ok   fixing the origin is not enough: the stored entry keeps leaking until it expires or is purged
   [cache] purge url /members/me: 1 entries
   [cache] purge url /help/contributions: 1 entries
   purge: {"purged":1} for /members/me, {"purged":1} for /help/contributions
   member 2 after the purge: Bruno Lefèvre [PASS, Cache-Control: private, no-cache], again: Bruno Lefèvre [PASS]
   ok   after the fix and the purge, member 2 sees their own page, never stored (PASS), and French readers get French

## 6. Data changes: waiting for the TTL versus event-driven invalidation
   concept: with only a TTL a price change waits up to s-maxage (+ stale-while-revalidate); with the outbox the cache purges the tag at commit, so the TTL can stay long and the hit ratio high
   [cache] invalidation off: entries live until their TTL
   [cache] purge everything: 3 entries
   fund 1 price 109.5275 [MISS]; 400 s later, nothing changed: [REVALIDATED], origin answered {"/api/funds 304":1}
   ok   past s-maxage + stale-while-revalidate the cache revalidates with If-None-Match, and the origin answers 304
   UPDATE fund_prices: fund 1 is now 120.4803 in Postgres (invalidation off)
     right after: 109.5275 [HIT, Age 0]
     +290 s: 109.5275 [HIT, Age 290]
     +20 s (age 310, stale): 109.5275 [STALE, Age 310]
     next request: 120.4803 [HIT, Age 0]
   ok   with only the TTL the old price is served for 300 s, then once more while revalidating (stale-while-revalidate), then the new one
   [cache] invalidation on: LISTEN cache_invalidations, outbox after #1
   [cache] outbox #2 (UPDATE on fund_prices): purged tag funds, 1 entries, 2 ms after the change
   invalidation on: 120.4803 [HIT] -> UPDATE (now 126.5043) -> 126.5043 [MISS] 248 ms after the commit
   ok   with the outbox the next request after the commit misses and gets the new price within a second
   the cache's LISTEN connection drops (pg_terminate_backend), and a price changes while it is gone:
   [cache] invalidation connection lost; reconnecting and replaying the outbox after #2
   [cache] outbox #3 (UPDATE on fund_prices): purged tag funds, 1 entries, 289 ms after the change
   price 122.7092 served [MISS] 374 ms after the commit: the NOTIFY was lost, the outbox row was not
   ok   after reconnecting, the cache replays the outbox from the last id it saw and purges
   ok   every change left one outbox row

